<!-- Notes 
	Target is the target animation state of the transition. This is a mandatory parameter. If you want to describe a transition from a current state to a non state for exqample a secondary animation back to fallback state then Target should take the special value "none" 
	Source is the source animation state of the transition. This is an optional parametar unless the target state is set as "none".  
	Resource	is the resource name of the animation entity. This is an optional parameter. You can specify an actual resource type or a resource branch. for example r_player races will cover all player races. If you leave this blank then the rule will apply for all animated entities
	
	Transition is the time it takes to transition to the target state expressed in percent of the target animation duration (i.e. 0.3 =30%). If the target animation is "none" then it will be the percent of the source animation duration 

	use /anim_reload_transitions chat command to reload this file into memory 
	
	in case some transition rules overlap the following prioritization takes place 
target animation state + source animation state 			> target animation state 
target animation state + resource 							> target animation state 
target animation state + source animation state + resource 	> all other combinations 
target animation state + resource 							> target animation state + source animation state 
	
-->
